From: Catalyst Linux
Subject: [PATCH] cardputerzero-v5: keep the backlight dark until the shell draws

The backlight was forced on as its driver probed, before the panel was set
up, so the panel's power-on memory (noise) showed, and then black until
the first frame. Now it starts dark at level 0; the panel driver's enable
powers it on at that level, and the shell brings it up once there is a
picture.

--- a/modules/CardputerZero/cardputerzero-v5-overlay.dts	2026-11-20 17:37:09.283930314 -0800
+++ b/modules/CardputerZero/cardputerzero-v5-overlay.dts	2026-11-20 17:37:09.283930314 -0800
@@ -326,10 +326,14 @@
                     45000 45500 46000 46500 47000 47500 48000 48500 49000 49500
                     50000
                 >;
-                default-brightness-level = <75>;
+                /*
+                 * Catalyst Linux: dark until the shell has drawn its first
+                 * frame and brings the light up to the level kept in its
+                 * settings. Lit at probe, the panel showed what its memory
+                 * held from power-on before it was set up.
+                 */
+                default-brightness-level = <0>;
                 power-supply = <&backlight_power>;
-                /* Force the backlight on during initialization */
-                force-enable-on-init;
             };
 
             spk_mute_switch: spk-mute-switch {
